    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (86.38) and **James Wood** (78.41) serve as our primary engines. **Corbin Carroll** is an absolute lock against Mitch Keller, as the combination of his elite speed and the favorable 4.67 xERA matchup maximizes his upside in our scarcity-driven categories. **James Wood** is similarly positioned for an elite performance; facing a struggling Max Scherzer (5.89 xERA) with a top-tier .420 xwOBA, he provides the most significant leverage of the day. We are also capitalizing on **Jose Caballero** (69.60), whose 13% platoon boost against a left-handed arm creates a high-ceiling play that outweighs the caution required by a lower batting order slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Henry Bolte** (47.92), who pushed toward the threshold but ultimately lacked the lineup security to supplant our starters. While **Henry Bolte** benefits from a strong park factor and platoon edge, his projected spot at the bottom of the order (-8% penalty) and the lack of confirmed status forced the optimizer to favor the higher floor provided by **Edwin Arroyo** and **Austin Riley**. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the weather, as **Zach McKinstry** remains on the bench not only due to his lower score but also the 31% rain risk clouding his matchup against Kyle Bradish. With **Vinnie Pasquantino** off the board due to a team-wide off-day, we are leaning heavily on **Josh Naylor** (66.82) to anchor the utility spot against Rocker, ensuring we maintain our categorical volume while aggressively targeting the stolen base upside offered by **Brice Turang** and **Cole Young**.",
